// =====================================================================
// ESP32 SEWING OPERATION COUNTER  v2.4   -   1.8" ST7735 (160x128)
// =====================================================================
// WHAT THIS DEVICE DOES
//   One device sits on one sewing machine.
//   - An IR sensor tells it whether a garment (fabric) is under the needle.
//   - An NJK-5002C proximity sensor gives one pulse per stitch.
//   - When the operator REMOVES the garment, the device looks at how many
//     stitches were made and decides:  GOOD (FG)  /  SHORT reject  /  OVER.
//   - v2.4 RFID ROUTING: the operator scans an OPERATION CARD at the machine.
//     The server links this machine to that operation of the style (e.g.
//     M07 = Op 2 of PM666/01). Each style has a route Op 1 -> Op 10.
//   - When ANY machine finishes a good piece of Op 1, the machine(s) on Op 2
//     see IN +1 within ~3 seconds. IN = pieces waiting from the previous op.
//     (IN = FG of previous operation - FG of this operation, shared by all
//     machines that run the same operation.)
//   - IN RULE (set per style in the app):
//       WARN  = count even when IN is 0, but show "NO INPUT" (default)
//       BLOCK = stitches are ignored while IN is 0 ("WAITING FOR PIECES")
//
// STITCH CONDITION (example: MIN 40, TARGET 50, MAX 55)
//   stitches on removal   result
//   ------------------    -----------------------------------------------
//    0                    nothing (garment placed and removed, no sewing)
//    1 .. 39   (< MIN)    SHORT  -> REJECT +1          (2 beeps, red)
//   40 .. 55   (MIN..MAX) GOOD   -> FG +1, QTY -1      (1 beep, green)
//   56 +       (> MAX)    OVER   -> REJECT +1          (supervisor can set
//                                   "ACCEPT" instead -> FG +1 but logged as over)
//   While sewing:  at 50 (TARGET) -> 1 beep, "TARGET - REMOVE"
//                  at 56 (MAX+1)  -> 3 beeps, red "OVER LIMIT - REMOVE"
//
// TFT pins & fonts are set in TFT_eSPI/User_Setup.h
//   TFT: MOSI23 SCLK26 CS5 DC16 RST17
//
// WIRING
//   IR sensor output  -> GPIO 19
//   NJK-5002C output  -> optocoupler -> GPIO 34 (input-only pin: add 10k
//                        pull-up to 3.3V; idles HIGH, pulse = LOW)
//   Buzzer            -> GPIO 22
//   RDM6300 RFID (125 kHz) TX -> GPIO 27   (RDM6300 runs on 5 V, its TX is
//                        5 V: use a 1k/2k divider to make it 3.3 V)
//   NEVER feed the 12-24 V NJK-5002C output straight into an ESP32 pin.
//
// Libraries: TFT_eSPI only (Wi-Fi, HTTP and OTA come with the ESP32 core)
// Board: ESP32 Dev Module.  Partition scheme must have OTA
//   ("Default 4MB with spiffs" is fine)
// =====================================================================

